# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 1 (market data + spread observer) uses ONLY public WebSocket/REST
# endpoints. No API keys are required or read in Phase 1.
#
# The variables below are documented ahead of Phase 2/3 so key provisioning
# can be prepared correctly. When you create keys:
#   * TRADE-ONLY permission. Withdrawals DISABLED. Transfers DISABLED.
#   * IP whitelist locked to the machine running this system.
#   * One key pair per venue, per environment (paper vs live).
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored). Never commit real keys.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Phase 3 live-trading interlock (unused in Phase 1; documented for later)
# Live trading will require BOTH the --live CLI flag AND this variable set to
# the exact string shown. Either one alone must refuse to trade live.
# ARB_CONFIRM_LIVE_TRADING=I_UNDERSTAND_THE_RISKS

# --- Binance (global) --------------------------------------------------------
# BINANCE_API_KEY=
# BINANCE_API_SECRET=

# --- Bybit -------------------------------------------------------------------
# BYBIT_API_KEY=
# BYBIT_API_SECRET=

# --- OKX (global) ------------------------------------------------------------
# OKX_API_KEY=
# OKX_API_SECRET=
# OKX_API_PASSPHRASE=

# --- Bitget ------------------------------------------------------------------
# BITGET_API_KEY=
# BITGET_API_SECRET=
# BITGET_API_PASSPHRASE=
